      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm trying to understand the thermodynamic cycle of a turbocharger better. can u explain how the enthalpy of the exhaust gas is actually converted into kinetic energy to drive the turbine wheel? specifically, i'm curious about the role of the volute and how the pressure differential across the turbine housing facilitates that energy transfer to the compressor side. i want to get into the actual physics of the gas flow, not just a general overview.",
